# Copy to deploy/docker/.env and fill in before `docker compose up`.
#
# IMPORTANT: as of this file, NONE of these are read by any Go binary
# in this repo — grep for `os.Getenv\|viper\.` under internal/ and cmd/
# to confirm; internal/config is a minimal struct with no env/file
# loading wired yet. They are here as the intended interface docker-compose.yml
# plumbs through to the cerberus-api/worker/mcp containers, documented
# honestly ahead of that wiring landing (see docs/deployment/team.md).

# --- Database (Postgres) ---
# Not read by any binary yet. internal/storage also has no Postgres
# implementation yet — see docs/deployment/team.md for the gap.
CERBERUS_DB_NAME=cerberus
CERBERUS_DB_USER=cerberus
CERBERUS_DB_PASSWORD=change-me-before-any-real-use

# --- Secret handling (see docs/adr/0001-no-raw-secret-storage.md) ---
# The HMAC key internal/policy.Fingerprinter needs. `cerberus scan file`
# generates an ephemeral random one per CLI invocation today (see
# cmd/cerberus/scan.go's buildDetector) — a real deployment needs a
# STABLE key so the same secret fingerprints the same way across runs.
# Not yet read by any binary; treat this as a placeholder for where
# that wiring will read from, and never commit a real value here.
CERBERUS_FINGERPRINT_KEY=change-me-to-a-random-32-byte-value-before-any-real-use

# --- Local LLM (optional — see docs/architecture/llm-non-sovereign.md) ---
# Every service must keep working with this unset/unreachable.
CERBERUS_OLLAMA_ENDPOINT=http://ollama:11434
